<Base title="Privacy" description="What Find Me CBR keeps, and what it doesn't.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p><strong>Draft for legal review before launch.</strong></p>
    <p>You don't need an account to use Find Me CBR, and we don't use advertising trackers.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Searches and taps:</strong> we keep daily totals, such as how often a search found nothing. We don't keep records of what any one person searched for.</li>
      <li><strong>Near me:</strong> your browser asks first. Your location stays in your browser for that visit, and isn't sent to us.</li>
      <li><strong>Forms:</strong> when you send a correction, suggestion or claim, we keep what you send so we can check it. <em>[How long we keep it goes here.]</em></li>
      <li><strong>Businesses:</strong> we publish business contact details, but never a private home address.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><em>[Contact details for privacy questions go here.]</em></p>
  </div>
</Base>
